<p>The United States imposed sanctions Tuesday on 35 individuals and entities that it said helped Iran’s shadow banking sector move the equivalent of tens of billions of dollars tied to sanctions evasion, oil sales and what Washington calls Tehran’s support for terrorism. The Treasury Department said the network allowed Iran’s armed forces, including the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps, to receive payment for illicit oil sales, procure sensitive components for missile programs and transfer funds to groups Washington considers terrorist. Treasury also warned banks against doing business with any firm paying Iran’s government or the IRGC for passage through the Strait of Hormuz, saying such transactions could carry significant sanctions risk. OFAC singled out independent Chinese “teapot” refineries, primarily in Shandong province, because of their role in importing and refining Iranian oil, and CNBC reported that the alert said China buys about 90% of Iran’s oil exports, with teapot refineries accounting for most of those imports. The measures are part of the Trump administration’s “Economic Fury” campaign, which Treasury has used to increase financial pressure on Tehran during the Iran conflict. Aaj TV reported that efforts to end the two-month Iran war remained at an impasse Tuesday, with President Trump unhappy with Tehran’s latest proposal to defer discussion of its nuclear program until the conflict ended and shipping disputes were resolved.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/ASAIO8ovi4mIUSHdy2Qc9hCjOGr93cjlIlUnU0BTUV08Koe0eXZYQ3iYgTlCFe3at-IZwLbYPxZtMLIh9_-WNbUAXTbJSFFiBlFHr0q6tliKrvgAFcNUiZ1fXzjh1Q8xtxOjEixWOKW3XqHViGQb3XbnUqDGp0r6V7GJe5gH-8vAVpIkn2AqVrcCSUC40NRP3RKM9LyHosM' alt='Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent, whose department announced new sanctions targeting Iranian oil exports and shadow banking networks.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Scope of the FAQ: OFAC said the restriction applies to direct and indirect payments by U.S. persons, U.S. financial institutions and U.S.-owned or controlled foreign entities, and that non-U.S. payers can also face sanctions exposure.</li><li>Named refineries: Treasury guidance cited five already-sanctioned Chinese teapot refineries: Shandong Shouguang Luqing Petrochemical, Shandong Shengxing Chemical, Hebei Xinhai Chemical, Shandong Jincheng Petrochemical and Hengli Petrochemical Refinery.</li><li>Bank outreach: The guidance suggested that financial institutions communicate with Chinese banks about sanctions risks and gather additional information on relevant customers and transactions.</li><li>Targeted firms: JNS reported that Tuesday’s designations included Farab Soroush Afagh Qeshm Company, two of its senior executives, firms linked to Bank Sina and Bank Sepah, and Nix Energy and Tai Lung Trading.</li></ul><blockquote>Iran&#x27;s shadow banking system serves as a critical financial lifeline for its armed forces, enabling activities that disrupt global trade and fuel violence across the Middle East - Scott Bessent</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. Treasury Department: Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said financial institutions that facilitate or engage with Iran’s shadow banking networks risk “severe consequences.” (<a href='https://www.jns.org/news/u-s-news/trump-admin-sanctions-iranian-shadow-banking-sector'>JNS</a>)</li><li>U.S. State Department: State Department spokesperson Tommy Pigott said the designations were part of dismantling Iran’s financial channels under Washington’s maximum-pressure approach. (<a href='http://beijingbulletin.com/news/279017606/us-hits-iran-shadow-banking-network-with-new-sanctions'>Beijing Bulletin</a>, <a href='https://www.radiosvoboda.org/a/news-iran-sanktsiyi-ssha/33744582.html'>Radio Svoboda</a>)</li><li>China: China has said it opposes what it calls “illegal” unilateral sanctions. (<a href='https://tribune.com.pk/story/2605395/us-imposes-sanctions-on-35-individuals-entities-for-aiding-irans-sanctions-evasions'>The Express Tribune</a>)</li><li>U.S. Treasury guidance to banks: Semafor reported that the alert is part of a broader Treasury push dubbed “Economic Fury,” a play on the military’s “Operation Epic Fury.” (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/28/2026/treasury-directs-banks-to-steer-clear-of-chinas-teapot-refineries'>Semafor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-imposes-sanctions-on-35-individuals-entities-for-aiding-irans-sanctions-evasions/article70918943.ece'>U.S. imposes sanctions on 35 individuals, entities for aiding Iran&#x27;s sanctions evasions</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/us-imposes-sanctions-on-35-individuals-entities-for-aiding-irans-sanctions-evasions'>US imposes sanctions on 35 individuals, entities for aiding Iran’s sanctions evasions</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/28/us/politics/treasury-iran-oil-sanctions.html'>Treasury Issues More Sanctions on Iranian Oil Exports</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/28/2026/treasury-directs-banks-to-steer-clear-of-chinas-teapot-refineries'>Treasury directs banks to steer clear of China’s ‘teapot’ refineries</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://tribune.com.pk/story/2605395/us-imposes-sanctions-on-35-individuals-entities-for-aiding-irans-sanctions-evasions'>US imposes sanctions on 35 individuals, entities for aiding Iran&#x27;s sanctions evasions</a> - tribune.com.pk</li><li><a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330457602/us-hits-iran-with-new-sanctions-targeting-shadow-banking-network'>US hits Iran with new sanctions targeting shadow banking network</a> - aaj.tv</li><li><a href='https://www.israelnationalnews.com/news/426247'>US sanctions 35 Iranian entities in &#x27;shadow banking&#x27; crackdown</a> - israelnationalnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rbc.ua/rus/news/ssha-rozshirili-sanktsiyi-proti-iranu-ta-1777414481.html'>США 